# A spell's SIBLING clause protects the bearer's gear (bd inc-w26h).
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/gear-spell-protection.keys 5
#
# WHAT IS BEING MEASURED. "Endure the Elements" (lib/wspells.irh:5645) carries
# Flags: EF_PROTECTS_ITEMS in its FIRST clause, whose grant is AD_SONI. The
# AD_ACID grant this session strikes lives in the fourth `and EA_INFLICT`
# sibling clause. Creature::GearResistLevel (src/Values.cpp) reads the flag off
# the TEffect the stati's eID names, so the session answers one question: does a
# sibling clause's stati name the same flagged TEffect as the first clause's?
#
# WHY A MAGE AT LEVEL TEN. The spell is level 4, so a mage needs level 7 to hold
# a slot for it. Its pval is 3d1 + (LEVEL_1PER2), so the resistance is 3 + half
# the caster level: 8 at level ten. The arithmetic below needs 6; ten is taken
# for margin and because the sheet then reads a round "Acid 8".
#
# WHY A SILVERED MAGIC WARHAMMER. src/Fight.cpp:2122 sets ignoreHardness when a
# no-save A_DEQU strikes a NON-magical item, and since inc-kapn
# src/Item.cpp:1468 zeroes only what Hardness() returned, with the owner's grant
# added after it at src/Item.cpp:1481. A resistance therefore survives on a
# mundane weapon too; this session buys a magic one for its numbers. "Warhammer,
# Dwarven Thrower" arrives from the wizard menu at its INITIAL_PLUS of +2
# (lib/m_items.irh:6861), which is magic and has 45 base hit points (weight 120,
# lang/Grammar.acc:577). IQ_SILVER makes it silver, whose acid hardness is 5,
# halved to 2 by the same quality (src/Item.cpp:1361), leaving 2 + 5 x 2 = 12
# for the plus.
#
# WHY A MAGMA CREEPER. Its A_DEQU is 3d6 AD_ACID with NO save DC
# (lib/mon3.irh:2828), so no Reflex roll decides the outcome and hardness is the
# only thing between the acid and the hammer. 12 + 8 = 20 exceeds the 18 the
# dice can reach, so the protection is decisive rather than lucky, while the
# bare 12 lets a roll of 13 or better through. It has 12 HD and resists blunt,
# so one creeper survives twelve blows; frozen monsters still answer a hit.
#
# The oracle is the game's own combat-numbers line (src/Item.cpp:1511-1531),
# which prints the hardness AFTER the owner's gear resistance is added:
#   "Warhammer, Dwarven Thrower +2: 3d6 Acid = 5 vs. 20 (silver) [unhurt]"
# 20 is 12 + 8. Without the flag the same line reads "vs. 12 (silver)".

@include chargen-mage.keys

# chargen-mage.keys stops on the arrival room description. Dismiss it, or the
# [w] below is eaten by the description.
ESC

# Wizard switches, counted from the top of the list in src/Tables.cpp:2680:
#   1 Cheat Death, 3 Free Advancement, 6 Ignore Spell Failure,
#   8 Infinite Mana, 11 Freeze Monsters. A frozen monster takes no turn of its
# own but still ANSWERS a blow, which is the whole point of an A_DEQU check.
w
y
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
SPACE
DOWN*2
SPACE
DOWN*3
SPACE
DOWN*2
SPACE
DOWN*3
SPACE
ESC

# Nine free levels, on the character screen: 'd' opens it and 'G' gains a level.
# The three @while guards answer the three prompts a mage meets on the way up;
# the metamagic one arrives at level five and is easy to forget, and a level-up
# prompt left unanswered swallows every key after it. SPACE, not ESC, leaves the
# character screen (src/Managers.cpp:2517-2518).
d
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
G
@while "Bonus To Which Attribute" a
@while "Choose a feat" a
@while "Choose a bonus metamagic Feat" a
@while "You feel" ESC
SPACE

# Teach the mage the one spell this fixture needs. Know All Spells is not used:
# it fills the Spell Manager with pages of spells and @choose reads only what is
# on the screen.
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Endure the Elements"
ENTER

# Cast it on the caster himself. "*" targets self.
m
@choose "Endure the Elements"
*
@while "more --" SPACE

# --- the weapon whose hit points are measured ---
# ENTER at the item-level prompt keeps the effect's own INITIAL_PLUS of +2.
w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*10
@until "Dwarven Thrower" DOWN
DOWN
ENTER
@expect "Enter Item Level"
ENTER
b
SPACE
@while "two-handed" y
s                       # stow the starting knife the swap pushed into the air
@until "Things in View" ESC

w
@choose "Add Quality to Weapon"
"IQ_SILVER"
ENTER
@until "Things in View" ESC

# The plus is unknown to the character until it is identified, and an
# unidentified item's page hides its hit points.
w
@choose "Identify Whole Pack"
@until "Things in View" ESC

# The character sheet's Resistances page, as evidence that the sibling clause's
# grant is really on the character, at the magnitude the arithmetic needs.
d
@until "Resistances and Armour" DOWN
@dump:spell-sheet
@until "Things in View" ESC

@until "SPACE:Swap" i
@until ">>b)Weapon" b
@until "base value of" x
@dump:spell-before
@until "Things in View" ESC

# One creeper for all twelve blows. Its body is gargantuan, so the summon
# cursor's square is not where the body's western edge lands; the character
# walks east until he bumps into it, and every RIGHT after that is a blow.
w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Jellies"
@choose "magma creeper"
RIGHT*4 ENTER

RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-01
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-02
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-03
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-04
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-05
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-06
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-07
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-08
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-09
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-10
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-11
RIGHT
@while "Attack the" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:spell-strike-12

@until "SPACE:Swap" i
@until ">>b)Weapon" b
@until "base value of" x
@dump:spell-after
@until "Things in View" ESC
@quit
